\DOC ASSUME_CALLEE_SAFETY_TAILED_TAC

\TYPE {ASSUME_CALLEE_SAFETY_TAILED_TAC : thm -> string -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Adds to the goal's assumptions a labelled instance of a callee safety theorem,
with its existentially quantified event function replaced by a fresh named
function and its event trace generalised by an extra universally quantified
tail variable.

\DESCRIBE
The first argument {safety_th : thm} is the callee's safety specification, an
existentially quantified {ensures} statement about the event trace; the second,
{name : string}, is the label under which the derived assumption is placed in
the assumption list. The conclusion is unchanged, and the added assumption
{th'} is the body of {safety_th} with its leading existential witness
instantiated to a freshly generated event-function constant and with an extra
trailing universally quantified trace variable appended to the quantifier
prefix, so that the pre- and post-condition trace equalities are stated
relative to that trace being appended to the original one. Existing
assumptions, including ones added by earlier applications, are retained.
{
           A ?- t
   ======================  ASSUME_CALLEE_SAFETY_TAILED_TAC safety_th name
        A, th' ?- t
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces this single kind of outcome occurs, always on goals
whose conclusion is an existentially quantified {ensures}-style safety
statement.

\ENDDOC
